      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BROOKLYN DAN (1) was first up for 10 weeks when he came from a wide barrier for second to race rival SOHO TRUMP when fresh. Has won second up before so should be improved and strikes at 50 per cent here. The ace draw gives him the chance to turn the tables. SOHO TRUMP (2) is racing very well this preparation and is hard to knock after leading throughout to score easily here last time, his fourth success in five starts so far this campaign. Expect him to go forward again so he could continue on his winning way. LE CARDINAL (3) disappointed in the Vicbred Final last start but had won in the first two rounds of that series. Draws well so is worth another chance. BETTORLEFTALONE (8) has been runner-up in both starts off a spell. Won his lone third-up attempt so should be peaking and draws to trail the top pick. Could be dangerous.",
